# 🔍 Trusted OSINT Tools & Sources for Global Pulse

**Last Updated**: May 21, 2026

Curated list of free/public tools and accounts for monitoring geopolitics, conflicts (especially Middle East), terrorism, shipping, and markets.

---

## 🗺️ Conflict & Geopolitics Monitoring

- **[Liveuamap](https://liveuamap.com)** — Real-time conflict maps and news aggregation
- **[DeepStateMap](https://deepstatemap.live)** — Excellent for ongoing wars and military movements
- **[World Monitor](https://worldmonitor.app)** — Interactive global dashboard with conflict layers, flights, and AI briefs
- **[SignalCockpit](https://signalcockpit.com)** — Strong for Middle East/Iran monitoring
- **[USvsIRAN.com](https://usvsiran.com)** — Focused OSINT dashboard for US-Iran related developments
- **[MarineTraffic](https://www.marinetraffic.com)** — Live ship tracking (critical for Red Sea, Hormuz, etc.)
- **[Flightradar24](https://www.flightradar24.com)** — Real-time aircraft tracking

## 📡 News & Social Media Monitoring

- **Google Alerts** — Set custom alerts for keywords
- **Google Trends** — Track rising topics and search interest
- **[Social Searcher](https://www.social-searcher.com)** — Search across multiple social platforms
- **X/Twitter Advanced Search** — Powerful for real-time OSINT

### Recommended X/Twitter Accounts (Follow & Monitor)
- @sentdefender (OSINTdefender) — Strong on Middle East conflicts
- @Osinttechnical — Technical OSINT updates
- @AuroraIntel — Middle East-focused with verification
- @WarMonitors — Breaking conflict news
- @Osint613 — Global & Middle East real-time monitoring

## 📈 Markets & Economic Intelligence

- Official exchange sites (Yahoo Finance, TradingView, Bloomberg free sections)
- UN Comtrade — Global trade data
- MarineTraffic + shipping indices for trade disruptions
- Google Alerts for commodity keywords (Oil, Gold, etc.)

## 🛠️ General OSINT Frameworks & Toolkits

- **[OSINT Framework](https://osintframework.com)** — Massive directory of tools
- Maltego (Community edition available)
- Shodan — Search for internet-connected devices
- theHarvester, Recon-ng, SpiderFoot (for advanced users)

## ⚠️ Important Guidelines
- Always **cross-verify** information from multiple sources
- Clearly mark unverified claims or paid content
- Add date + source link for every update in Daily Brief
- Stay neutral and factual

